CRITICAL — start() MUST pass (resolve, reject) to the Promise executor and call server.on('error', reject). Without reject, EADDRINUSE hangs the Promise forever — undetectable by tests unless explicitly awaited with a timeout. Also validate port in constructor: Number.isInteger(port) && port >= 0 && port <= 65535.

CRITICAL — src/index.ts must NOT call app.listen() at the top level (outside a class/function). Only a class start() method or a module-main guard should bind a port. A bare top-level listen() fires on every import, causing port collisions in the test suite.

WRITE THE FILE FIRST — call your file-writing tool immediately with a complete implementation. Do not plan or reason before writing. Write the file now, then verify. CRITICAL — vitest.config.ts MUST include the pattern: include: ['src/**/*.test.ts']. Without this vitest picks up compiled dist/**/*.test.js files and fails with "Vitest cannot be imported in a CommonJS module". The correct vitest.config.ts:
  import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';
  export default defineConfig({ test: { globals: true, environment: 'node', include: ['src/**/*.test.ts'], passWithNoTests: true } });

CRITICAL — package.json MUST have a 'test' script. External verification runs 'npm test' and fails with exit 1 if the script is missing. Required scripts section:
  "scripts": { "start": "node dist/server.js", "build": "tsup", "test": "vitest run" }

