WRITE THE FILE FIRST — call your file-writing tool immediately with a complete implementation. Do not plan or reason before writing. Write the file now, then verify. CRITICAL — vitest 4.x mock constructor pattern: vi.fn() implementations must use REGULAR FUNCTION (not arrow) when the mock is called with new. Arrow functions in vi.fn(() => ...) cause vitest 4.x to return an empty this instead of the returned object, so client.searchFlights becomes undefined and all /search and /cheapest tests return 500.

CORRECT test file mock contract (mock path is './skyscanner/client' — a subdirectory):
  const { mockedSearchFlights, mockedCheapest } = vi.hoisted(() => ({
    mockedSearchFlights: vi.fn(),
    mockedCheapest: vi.fn(),
  }));
  vi.mock('./skyscanner/client', () => ({
    SkyscannerClient: vi.fn(function(this: any) {
      this.searchFlights = mockedSearchFlights;
      this.cheapest = mockedCheapest;
    }),
  }));

CRITICAL — The mock path MUST be './skyscanner/client' (subdirectory), NOT './skyscanner-client' (flat file). The flat file does not exist — using the wrong path causes Failed to load url and zero tests run.

CRITICAL — Use vi.hoisted() to create mockedSearchFlights and mockedCheapest BEFORE vi.mock() runs.

CRITICAL — DO NOT add 503 middleware that checks for RAPIDAPI_KEY. Tests do not set RAPIDAPI_KEY. Create SkyscannerClient inside each route handler (per-request), NOT at module level.

CRITICAL — Do NOT remove the 'test' script from package.json. Keep: "test": "vitest run".


CRITICAL — In beforeEach, use vi.clearAllMocks() NOT vi.resetAllMocks(). clearAllMocks() only clears call history; resetAllMocks() also wipes mock implementations. When resetAllMocks() is used, the SkyscannerClient constructor mock loses its implementation and new SkyscannerClient({}) no longer assigns this.searchFlights — all route handlers then throw 'client.searchFlights is not a function' causing 500 on every test. Use vi.clearAllMocks() to preserve the constructor implementation between tests.

CRITICAL — SearchParams fields are 'origin' and 'destination', NOT 'from' and 'to'. The server calls: client.searchFlights({ origin: from, destination: to, date, adults }). Test assertions MUST use { origin: ..., destination: ..., date: ..., adults: 1 } NOT { from: ..., to: ... }.

CRITICAL — Do NOT import from './skyscanner/types' — this file does not exist. Do not add FlightResult[] type annotation to mock flight arrays. Use: const flights = [...]

CRITICAL — Do NOT import 'cors' package — it is not installed. Use inline CORS middleware: app.use((req, res, next) => { res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', '*'); next(); }).

CRITICAL — Do NOT import FlightResult from './skyscanner/types' — this file does not exist. Import FlightResult from './skyscanner/client'.

